{"t": 1795092673.473975, "tool": "analyze", "code": "from scipy.optimize import least_squares\ndef model(p,t,A):\n    return -p[0]*t**p[1]*A**p[2]*np.exp(-p[3]*A)\nbest=None\nfor s in range(20):\n    p0=np.random.RandomState(s).uniform(-1,2,4)\n    try:\n        r=least_squares(lambda p: model(p,t,A)-dA_dt, p0)\n        if best is None or r.cost<best.cost: best=r\n    except Exception as e: pass\nprint(best.x, np.sqrt(np.mean(best.fun**2))/np.std(dA_dt))\nres=best.fun\nfor lo,hi in [(0,0.5),(0.5,1),(1,2),(2,3),(3,4.1)]:\n    m=(A>=lo)&(A<hi); print('A',lo,hi, np.round(np.mean(res[m]),3), np.round(np.std(res[m]),3))\nfor lo,hi in [(0,2),(2,4),(4,6),(6,8),(8,10.1)]:\n    m=(t>=lo)&(t<hi); print('t',lo,hi, np.round(np.mean(res[m]),3), np.round(np.std(res[m]),3))\n", "out": "[3.56759574 0.90651347 0.25277259 0.32867874] 0.24122392718592742\nA 0 0.5 0.42 1.351\nA 0.5 1 0.776 1.149\nA 1 2 0.203 0.631\nA 2 3 -0.275 0.725\nA 3 4.1 -0.868 1.652\nt 0 2 -0.781 2.017\nt 2 4 -0.191 1.464\nt 4 6 0.1 0.587\nt 6 8 0.102 0.32\nt 8 10.1 -0.006 1.055\n"}
